title: Return dedicated error for justifications signed by previous authority set
doc:
- audience: Todo
  description: |-
    # Description

    Return a dedicated error when a GRANDPA justification is signed by the previous authority set.

    - `bp-header-chain`: add `JustificationVerificationError::OutdatedAuthoritySet`. The strict   verifier (`verify_justification`) returns it when a precommit signature is valid for the   previous authority set.
    - `pallet-bridge-grandpa`: map this error to `Error::InvalidAuthoritySetId` instead of `Error::InvalidJustification`.
    - The optimizer (`verify_and_optimize_justification`) and the equivocations collector are unchanged. They still treat such votes as votes with an invalid signature.

    ## Integration

    - `bp-header-chain`: `JustificationVerificationError` has a new variant, `OutdatedAuthoritySet`.
      Code that matches on this enum exhaustively needs to handle it.
    - `pallet-bridge-grandpa`: `submit_finality_proof` and `submit_finality_proof_ex` return
      `InvalidAuthoritySetId` for justifications signed by the previous authority set.

    ## Review Notes

    - The private `JustificationVerifier` trait gets a `process_outdated_signature_vote` method. By default it calls `process_invalid_signature_vote`. Only the strict verifier overrides it.
    - Only the directly previous set is detected, same as `sp_consensus_grandpa::check_message_signature_with_buffer`. Signatures from older sets are still reported as `InvalidAuthoritySignature`.

    Tests added:
    - `justification_signed_by_previous_authority_set_rejected_as_outdated` (strict verifier)
    - `outdated_authority_signatures_are_removed_by_optimizer` (optimizer)
    - `rejects_justification_that_has_old_set_id` (pallet)
crates:
- name: pallet-bridge-grandpa
  bump: major
- name: bp-header-chain
  bump: major
